  "title": "Region 32 Dispatch",
  "subtitle": "Logistical Coordination Concerns Near Reed Camp",
  "main_story": {
    "headline": "Departure Timeline for Survey Team Remains Unconfirmed Despite Planning Efforts",
    "lede": "Discussions among local personnel focused on the departure schedule of the *survey team*, noting specific questions regarding time coordination and confirmation sources.",
    "body": "Logistical planning concerning the movement of the *survey team* concluded yesterday with several points of clarification needed. **Wren** initially stated that the group planned to depart following the second bell.\n\nThe timing immediately prompted a question from **Xara**, who noted the ambiguity surrounding the specified time, asking if \"that means the noon bell or evening bell.\" \n\nIn response, **Wren** redirected the need for confirmation, stating that **Yori** was expected to post the confirmed departure time. This exchange highlighted the immediate operational gap regarding scheduling certainty.\n\nFurther discussion from **Xara** established a key logistical detail, noting that \"The survey team is waiting at Reed Camp.\" The conversation thus focused on ensuring all parties are aware of both the current gathering location and the critical need for official confirmation on the departure schedule."
  }
}

